course: dictionary
lesson: 13266
title: Goatskin: skin, leather and drums
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are made of two smaller words joined together. Goatskin is goat and skin, so it means the skin of a goat. «The old man filled his goatskin with water from the well.» The word skin tells you it is a covering, and goat tells you whose skin it is.
explain: Goatskin can also mean something made from that skin. «She bought a soft goatskin bag for her birthday.» Here the goatskin is not the animal's skin on the animal: it is the leather that the bag is made from. Ask yourself: is this talking about the skin itself, or about a thing made from it?
explain: Read the words around goatskin for more clues. «The drummer tapped the goatskin drum with his hands.» A drum is something you play, so a goatskin drum is a drum with goat skin on it. The clues in the sentence show you the meaning even if you have never seen the word before.
fact: Goatskin means the skin of a goat.
fact: Goatskin is often made into leather, which is strong and soft.
fact: Goatskin can also mean something made from goat leather, such as a bag or a drum.
fact: Long ago, people carried water and wine in goatskin bottles.
fact: Many djembe drums, from West Africa, have goatskin tops.
exercise: «She bought a soft goatskin bag.» What is goatskin? | *The skin of a goat, often made into leather | A kind of wool from sheep | A bag made of cloth | A hard metal used for tools
exercise: «The drummer tapped the goatskin drum.» What is a goatskin drum? | A very large drum for a band | *A drum with goat skin on it | A drum that plays by itself | A drum made of metal
exercise: «The old man filled the goatskin with water.» What did the old man use to carry the water? | The man's hat | The path | *The goatskin | The well
test: «The soft goatskin gloves kept her hands warm.» What were the gloves made from? | *Goatskin | Wool from sheep | Plastic | Cotton
test: Is goatskin a noun, a verb or an adjective? Look at its job in «a goatskin bag». | A verb | A number | An adjective | *A noun
exam: «Ali filled his goatskin bottle at the spring before the long desert walk.» What did Ali carry his water in? | A tin can | A glass jar | *A bottle made from goat skin | A plastic bag
